# Tools and Libraries

This document contains tools, frameworks, and libraries relevant to **Safety and Rollback Mechanisms for Objective Misinterpretation in Agentic AI Systems**.

These tools can support the development, testing, evaluation, monitoring, and safety analysis of autonomous AI agents.

---

## 1. LangChain

**Category:** LLM and Agent Development Framework

**Purpose:**
LangChain is a framework for developing applications powered by large language models. It supports the creation of AI agents capable of reasoning, using tools, accessing external information, and executing multi-step workflows.

**Relevance to this project:**

LangChain can be used to develop experimental agentic AI systems for studying:

* Agent planning
* Tool use
* Multi-step execution
* Agent memory
* Human approval workflows
* Action monitoring

It can also be extended with custom safety layers that validate actions before execution.

**Official Website:**
https://www.langchain.com/

**Documentation:**
https://python.langchain.com/

**GitHub:**
https://github.com/langchain-ai/langchain

---

## 2. LangGraph

**Category:** Stateful Agent Workflow Framework

**Purpose:**
LangGraph is a framework for building stateful and long-running AI agent workflows.

It represents agent execution as a graph consisting of states and transitions.

**Relevance to this project:**

LangGraph is particularly useful for studying safety and rollback because agent execution can be organized into different states.

For example:

```text
User Objective
      ↓
Objective Validation
      ↓
Planning
      ↓
Safety Check
      ↓
Checkpoint
      ↓
Tool Execution
      ↓
Monitoring
      ↓
Safe?
 ↙         ↘
Yes         No
 ↓           ↓
Continue    Rollback
```

A state-based architecture can make it easier to introduce:

* Checkpoints
* Human approval
* Safety validation
* Execution interruption
* Error recovery
* Rollback mechanisms

**Official Website:**
https://www.langchain.com/langgraph

**Documentation:**
https://langchain-ai.github.io/langgraph/

**GitHub:**
https://github.com/langchain-ai/langgraph

---

## 3. Microsoft AutoGen

**Category:** Multi-Agent AI Framework

**Purpose:**
AutoGen is a framework for developing applications involving multiple AI agents that can communicate and collaborate with each other.

**Relevance to this project:**

AutoGen can be used to study:

* Multi-agent coordination
* Agent communication
* Human-agent interaction
* Agent supervision
* Task delegation

A separate safety or monitoring agent can potentially evaluate actions proposed by another agent.

For example:

```text
Planning Agent
      ↓
Proposed Action
      ↓
Safety Agent
      ↓
Safe?
 ↙         ↘
Yes         No
 ↓           ↓
Execute     Stop / Request Human Review
```

**Official Website:**
https://microsoft.github.io/autogen/

**GitHub:**
https://github.com/microsoft/autogen

