## 4. Guardrails AI

**Category:** AI Output Validation and Safety Framework

**Purpose:**
Guardrails AI provides mechanisms for validating and controlling outputs generated by AI systems.

It can be used to define requirements and validation rules for LLM outputs.

**Relevance to this project:**

Guardrails can support safety mechanisms such as:

* Output validation
* Structured output enforcement
* Policy checks
* Input validation
* Detection of invalid responses

For an agentic system, validation can occur before an output is converted into an action or tool call.

**Official Website:**
https://www.guardrailsai.com/

**Documentation:**
https://www.guardrailsai.com/docs

**GitHub:**
https://github.com/guardrails-ai/guardrails

---

## 5. NVIDIA NeMo Guardrails

**Category:** Conversational AI Safety Framework

**Purpose:**
NVIDIA NeMo Guardrails is an open-source toolkit for adding programmable safety and control mechanisms to AI applications.

It allows developers to define rules governing interactions between users, language models, tools, and external systems.

**Relevance to this project:**

It can be used to implement:

* Safety policies
* Conversation controls
* Tool-use restrictions
* Human intervention
* Output restrictions
* Runtime safety checks

These capabilities are relevant to preventing unsafe actions before they occur.

**Official Website:**
https://www.nvidia.com/en-us/ai-data-science/products/nemo/

**GitHub:**
https://github.com/NVIDIA-NeMo/Guardrails

---

## 6. OpenAI Evals

**Category:** AI Evaluation Framework

**Purpose:**
OpenAI Evals provides a framework for creating and running evaluations for AI systems.

Evaluations can be designed to measure whether an AI system behaves correctly under different scenarios.

**Relevance to this project:**

Safety evaluations can test:

* Objective following
* Instruction conflicts
* Unsafe actions
* Tool-use behavior
* Policy compliance
* Robustness

This is useful for identifying objective misinterpretation before an agent is deployed.

**Official Website:**
https://github.com/openai/evals

---

## 7. Inspect AI

**Category:** AI Evaluation Framework

**Purpose:**
Inspect AI is an open-source framework designed for evaluating AI models and AI agents.

It supports the creation and execution of structured evaluations.

**Relevance to this project:**

Inspect AI can be useful for evaluating:

* Agent behavior
* Multi-step reasoning
* Tool use
* Safety constraints
* Harmful behavior
* Agent trajectories

It can be combined with safety benchmarks such as AgentHarm.

**Official Website:**
https://inspect.aisi.org.uk/

**GitHub:**
https://github.com/UKGovernmentBEIS/inspect_ai

---

## 8. AI Safety Gridworlds

**Category:** Reinforcement Learning Safety Environment

**Purpose:**
AI Safety Gridworlds provides simple environments for studying common AI safety problems.

The environments include examples related to:

* Reward hacking
* Safe exploration
* Side effects
* Interruptibility
* Reward specification

**Relevance to this project:**

It provides controlled environments for understanding how an agent can optimize a reward while producing unintended outcomes.

This makes it useful for studying objective misinterpretation and reward hacking.

**Paper:**
https://arxiv.org/abs/1711.09883

**GitHub:**
https://github.com/google-deepmind/ai-safety-gridworlds

